       00      At least one program was found with the requested name.

       11      No program was found with the requested name.

NNOOTTEESS
       _p_i_d_o_f is actually the same program as kkiillllaallll55(8); the program  behaves
       according to the name under which it is called.

       When  ppiiddooff  is  invoked  with a full pathname to the program it should
       find the pid of, it is reasonably safe. Otherwise it is  possible  that
       it  returns  PIDs of running programs that happen to have the same name
       as the program you're after but are actually other programs. Note  that
       the  executable  name  of  running  processes  is calculated with rreeaadd‐‐
       lliinnkk(2), so symbolic links to executables will also match.

       Zombie processes or processes in disk sleep (states Z  and  D,  respec‐
       tively)  are  ignored,  as  attempts  to access the stats of these will
       sometimes fail.  The --zz flag (see above) tells ppiiddooff to try  to  detect
       these sleeping and zombie processes, at the risk of failing or hanging.


